      "snippet": "Assistant: Fair question, and worth pausing on. **Deipnon** (Greek: δεῖπνον, \"meal\" or \"supper\") is the last day of the lunar month in the Attic Greek calendar — the day the old moon is fully dark, just before the new crescent appears. In ancient Athens, it was the day of **Hekat",
